  "title": "Szabo-2026-neurons-10.1038/s41467-026-71502-z",
  "description": "Intraoperative local field potentials recorded with microelectrodes from the subthalamic nucleus of 13 patients with Parkinson's disease undergoing deep brain stimulation surgery. Patients performed a stop-signal reaction time task during recording. This derivative release provides the authors' filtered 250 Hz continuous LFP (0.5 Hz high-pass version) repackaged in BIDS with event annotations.",
  "methods_description": "Intraoperative STN microelectrode LFP was recorded during a stop-signal task, released as EEGLAB files at 250 Hz and high-pass filtered at 0.5 or 2 Hz. The 0.5 Hz version was converted to BrainVision float32 µV with unchanged values, and annotations were exported to events.tsv.",
